PolicyManagerCancelByVetoTest
├── When no attempt was ever recorded
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and ask no method.
├── When the attempt was cancelled
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and ask no method.
├── When the attempt was consumed
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and ask no method.
├── When the attempt id is not the live one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId carrying both ids and ask no method.
├── When the attempt was judged under another nonce
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_StaleAttempt carrying both nonces and ask no method.
├── When the attempt ignores stops
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_AttemptIgnoresPause carrying the id and ask no method.
├── When the method is not one the attempt used
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotUsed carrying the id and the method and never call it.
├── When the method is in the rule but the attempt did not use it
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotUsed and never call it.
├── When the method is the zero address
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotUsed.
├── When the pause read returns nothing
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped naming the method.
├── When the pause read returns false
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped.
├── When the pause read reverts
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped.
├── When the pause read reverts with true
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped.
├── When the pause read returns less than a word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped.
├── When the pause read returns a word other than true
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped.
├── When the pause read returns true and more
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped.
├── When the pause read returns a huge answer
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped on a gas budget that copying the answer would exhaust.
├── When the pause read writes state
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped and leave the method's storage untouched.
├── When the used method has no code
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped.
├── When no attempt waits and every other check fails
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
├── When the id the nonce the pause choice and the method all fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId.
├── When the nonce the pause choice and the method all fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_StaleAttempt.
├── When the pause choice and the method both fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_AttemptIgnoresPause.
├── When the method is unused and not stopped
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotUsed.
├── When a used method reports a stop
│   ├── It should set the attempt to Cancelled and keep the rest of its record.
│   ├── It should emit AttemptCancelled alone, naming the caller and the method, with no places.
│   ├── It should read no proof and make only static calls.
│   └── It should leave the setup and the attempt counter unchanged.
├── When another used method reports a stop
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodNotStopped naming the method named.
├── When the wait is over
│   └── It should cancel the attempt.
├── When the same veto is sent twice
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
├── When the account spends after the veto
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
└── When an attempt opens after the veto
    └── It should open the next id under the same setup nonce.
